      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To convert from rectangular coordinates to spherical coordinates, we need to use the following formulas:\n$\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2}$\n$\\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)$\n$\\phi = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right)$\nLet's plug in the values of $x = 0,$ $y = -3 \\sqrt{3}$, and $z = 3$:\n$\\rho = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 3^2}$ \n                  = $\\sqrt{27 + 9}$ \n                  = $\\sqrt{36}$ \n                  = 6 \n$\\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{-3 \\sqrt{3}}{0}\\right)$\nSince $\\tan^{-1}$ is undefined when the denominator is 0, we can simplify this to:\n$\\theta = \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}$ \n$\\phi = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{6}\\right)$\n                      = $\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\n                      = $\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ \nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates $(0, -3 \\sqrt{3}, 3)$ convert to spherical coordinates $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\boxed{(6, \\frac{3 \\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{3})}.$",
